<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Yi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 309 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Yi was a political strategist of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> who served as chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>. He promoted the 'horizontal alliance' (lianheng), persuading states to ally with Qin rather than unite against it. In 313 BCE he induced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-huai-of-chu">King Huai of Chu</a> to break his alliance with Qi by promising land, then broke the promise, and Chu's defeats in the wars that followed in 312 BCE greatly strengthened Qin.</p></div>
